R99 - Q-R88-2 (handoff 06 s F3 gap): shared spans and path-derived entry fields for TEAM-ART-keyed members inside the gen7 EB
archives, measured read-only so the re-key / rename contract can state what an archive-side rename would have to touch and what it
could never touch safely. Trees: X360 Legacy, PS3 Legacy, X360 NHL 15, PS3 NHL 15 (EB 0x00000400, 16-byte rows), PS3 NHL 12 / 13
(EB, the archive-backed kit titles). Every *.big under the tree root is listed with the R0 EB lister (eb_list.parse).

Per archive row: `block << 4` = offset, `size` = stored size, `w4` (unknown word), `path_hash` (last word). Measured here:
  H1 path_hash == djb2(path) under 4 variants (add / xor; as stored / lowercase) x 2 separators - which variant, how many rows;
  W4 what `w4` is: equals size? 0? monotone with row index? the member's decompressed size (chunkzip header 'chunkzip' u32 at +8?)
     - reported as a distribution, not a conclusion;
  SPAN duplicate spans (same offset, same size), overlapping spans (interval overlap with a different offset) - per archive;
  FAM team-art family classification by path grammar (handoff 04 s3): FE crest t{id} / s{id}, rink logo texlib_{id}_a_b, centerlogo_{id},
     puck_{id}, kits rendering/{jersey,pant,sock}/texlib_{style}_{id}_{variant}; nameplate grammar is a CANDIDATE (rendering_name*{id});
     for every team-art member: is its span shared with a member of a different id (any family) or with a non-team-art member;
     ids per family; members per id; archives per family.
Nothing is written; no member is decoded except reading 16 header bytes for the W4 test.
Usage: python r99_team_art_archive_spans.py <out.json> [--trees a,b] [--ps4 <inxp_00.big>]
